  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Minor in Public Administration"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Minors",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Minors",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/minors/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "The Minor in Public Administration is comprised of three types of courses. There are courses focused on government as a political actor which provide the students with insights into the nature of modern politics. There are policy courses which emphasize the various terrains on which government and organized interests interact. Finally, there are courses in administration. The Minor in Public Administration provides the student with a comprehensive overview of Canadian public administration and policy."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Administered by: Department of Politics and Public Administration"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Exclusions: This minor is not available to students in the following programs:"
    },
